      "id": "09",
      "title": "Booking Preparation & Customer Workflow",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "The 11-Step Customer Journey"
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 1 — Share the family requirement: Tell us the purpose of the inquiry, family circumstances, ancestor details, Gotra, preferred date, and participation pathway, whether the family wishes to participate Online, in person or through an approved representative."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 2 — Information collection and consent: Minimum required customer, participant, and ancestral details are collected under strict consent controls. This may include contact details, country and language, Karta or participant name, Gotra, ancestor names and relationships, known Tithi, special family instructions, accessibility needs and confidentiality preferences."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 3 — Ritual assessment: Requirement is reviewed for the appropriate ritual or service category, eligibility, Sankalp details, prescribed Vidhi, participation suitability, sacred locations and preparation needs. Religious questions and final ritual decisions remain with the verified and trusted Gayawal Panda."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 4 — Panda, date and participation availability: Verification of Gayawal Panda availability, date, location, and operational capacity."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 5 — Scope, quotation and approval: Customer reviews and approves formal quotation outlining charges, inclusions, exclusions, and deliverables before payment."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 6 — Invoice, official payment and Universal Reference ID: Invoice issued and unique Universal Reference ID generated for tracking updates, booking, and support."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 7 — Booking confirmation and correction: Recipient gets details on assigned Panda, India date/time, locations, and preparation lists. Immediate corrections reported if needed."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 8 — Pre-ritual coordination: Final reporting instructions, online joining links, customer-prepared items, or courier needs are coordinated."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 9 — Ritual execution: Officiating Gayawal Panda performs ceremony according to authorized scope while Connect Hub Co. manages operational support."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 10 — Completion and deliverables: Customer receives completion status, summary, certificate, photos/videos (where permitted), Prasad dispatch, or Vahi updates."
        },
        {
          "kind": "step",
          "text": "Step 11 — Support, modification and closure: Post-service support, modifications, and formal tracked closure."
        }
      ]
